how to get in a state of flow it's a  question I got from one of my readers  Donald Donald no chew or chew Donald  anyway it's a great question I wrote an  email and created a video on flow and  the importance of it and how crucial it  is for your business when you recognize  you're in a state of flow and that's  when things are going right you know it  feels right the project you're working  on you have to keep going with it it's  so important because this is where the  genius is gonna come from and when you  try to force something it doesn't work I  don't know if there's a way to  deliberately create flow because if you  try to force flow it's not going to  happen right but what you can do is give  yourself the conditions to create  something amazing being in the state of  flow is like create an art or it's like  being very creative you know if you come  down on people and say okay we're gonna  have a brainstorming session everybody  meet here we're gonna be creative right  now you don't get great ideas because  you can't force creativity you can't  force flow in my opinion but you can  give yourself to conditions that will  best lead to flow here's what I find  super helpful I give myself freedom  again when you try to force something  okay now I want to get into the state of  flow it's probably not gonna happen and  when you're stressed out when you're  under pressure when you have deadlines  coming up then it's also really hard to  get into flow because you've got  something crunching down on you I try to  build a business that is not reactionary  I tried to build a no-pressure company  so that myself and the people on my team  are free to explore are not crunched  down just putting out fires all the time  that's most companies right you're just  putting out one fire that's telling you  go in another fire now and you never  spend any time actually growing your  business so you want to try to reduce  those numbers of fires free up your time  allow you to focus on bigger picture  stuff  when you freed up your schedule you  freed up your time you freed up space in  your mind it allows your creativity to  enter it allows you to get into the  state of flow and when you get there you  have to run with it if I'm in flow if  I'm really feeling something if I am in  the zone on something I'm working on  I push everything else that I'm doing  I'll cancel meetings I'll push  appointments I'll push deadlines on  things because I need to finish what I'm  doing because if I don't finish it now  it's gonna take me ten times as long on  another day and it won't be as good if I  ride with this genius right now what I'm  gonna end up with is amazing and as  entrepreneurs we don't get into flow  that often right it's not like every day  you're in flow if you're writing a week  of great flow you are lucky a lot of  times we are stuck forcing ourselves to  do something and that's important for a  business but the real growth is going to  come when you are in that state of flow  it starts by opening up your schedule so  leave time every day for what I call CEO  time this is where there's nothing  assigned you're gonna work on something  to grow your business but you don't have  a fixed project or something that you  have to get done take breaks off I like  to break my day into 90 minute chunks  and then take 15-minute breaks in  between and I'll go outside go for a  walk whatever it is just clear my head  I'm taking those breaks refreshes my  mind do something active physical I love  salsa dancing I do that 20 hours a week  and I get most of my best ideas most of  my creative ideas when I'm not in the  office sitting down in front of my  computer  maybe I'm the strange one but if you're  like me then you've got to get out you  know you get your ideas we need in a  shower you get your ideas when you're  you're going for a walk when you're  doing some kind of physical activity and  went on vacation when you're relaxing  how many times did you go away on a  vacation and come back with a million  different ways to grow your business  then that's a big idea to help you take  off  because you were relaxed and not under  huge amounts of pressure so again I  don't think you can force flow you can't  say flow right now bring it we're gonna  do something but you can create the  conditions that will bring it out to the  best of your abilities and it starts  with having as open as schedule as  possible and having a no crisis business  belief if you guys like this video  please leave a thumbs up below thank you  for the great question and if you have a  question for your company leave a  comment I'll do a video response I love  seeing you guys I love answering your  questions that makes my Wednesday every  week when I sit down here and I'm  recording these videos I love hearing  from you please leave something below  thank you so much and I'll see you soon
 

